According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global harvesting machinery market was valued at USD 31.8 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 48.9 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 4.6% during the forecast period (2025–2034). This growth is propelled by the rising mechanisation in emerging economies, expanding arable land area and the adoption of precision farming technologies that boost machine productivity.
Harvesting machinery comprises equipment designed for the efficient collection of mature crops, including combine harvesters, forage harvesters, cotton pickers and grape harvesters. These machines integrate cutting, threshing, cleaning and grain handling functions, enabling large scale producers to reduce labor intensity while improving yield quality.
